{"format":"hologram.registry.artifact/v1","id":"mcr.microsoft.com/azurelinux/base/tensorflow","fetched":"2026-09-25T12:12:08.504Z","source":{"name":"Microsoft Artifact Registry","api":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/api/v1/catalog/azurelinux/base/tensorflow/details?reg=mar","page":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/en-us/product/azurelinux/base/tensorflow/about"},"readme":"## About\n\nThis repository contains the official TensorFlow image for Azure Linux.\n\n### What is Azure Linux?\n\nAzure Linux is a Linux distribution for Microsoft’s cloud infrastructure and edge products and services. Azure Linux is designed to provide a consistent platform for these devices and services and will enhance Microsoft’s ability to stay current on Linux updates.  \n\nTo learn more about Azure Linux, refer to our [GitHub repository](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/).\n\n### What is TensorFlow?\n\nTensorFlow is an end-to-end open source platform for machine learning. It has a comprehensive, flexible ecosystem of tools, libraries, and community resources that lets researchers push the state-of-the-art in ML and developers easily build and deploy ML-powered applications.\n\nSee: [TensorFlow](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TensorFlow)\n\n## Featured tags\n\n- `2`\n\nNote: The featured tags are **not** multi-architecture tags as the image is only built for `x86-64` architecture. The tags refer to the latest version of the image. Additional tags that are specific to the TensorFlow version or Azure Linux build can be found in the Tags section.\n\n## Usage\n\nThe TensorFlow image ships with a bash shell. The following command will launch the shell:\n\n    docker run -it --rm mcr.microsoft.com/azurelinux/base/tensorflow:2 bash\n\n## Support\n\nAzure Linux container images are supported only for internal Microsoft use. For more information please see our [Support Statement](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/blob/-/SUPPORT.md).\n\n## License\n\nThe Azure Linux distribution is provided under the 